# No fallbacks before production

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 convention.

## Use This When

- A change could keep the old path "just in case", add a legacy toggle, or support two versions at once.

## Stop Here If

- There is exactly one active path.

## Core rule

- Until the first production release there is one active version of every mechanism. Replace, do not branch.
- No silent fallbacks: when a required capability is missing, fail with a message that names it instead of degrading quietly.
